<title>FRANCE: French raw steel output fell 2.8 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>French raw steel output fell 2.8 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>French raw steel production fell 2.8 percent to 17.599 million tonnnes in the full year 1996 over 1995, statistics from the French steel federation showed.</p>
<p>Output jumped 29.5 percent to 1.415 million tonnes in December 1996 from December 1995.</p>
<p>But production had hit an unusual low in December 1995, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
